                <mxCell id="cCFKwo3Y45gqiVWlcszK-22" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="Offsets don’t follow longitude exactly. Governments choose their own zones (China uses one time zone across a huge area), and some places use half-hour or 45-minute offsets, like India (+5:30) and Nepal (+5:45)." vertex="1">
